<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Oct 12.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Oct 12.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended Oct 12</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE    % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				 (RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>State Bank	   215	   0.56     637950 137.16    13.58</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   174	   0.37     324900  56.53    11.09</p>
<p>Reliance	     193	   0.50     245150  47.31    13.51</p>
<p>L&amp;T		    215	   0.53     140500  30.21    12.85</p>
<p>Tata Power	   121	   0.29     207600  25.12    12.50</p>
<p>ACC		   1725	   2.81	13480  23.25     8.49</p>
<p>Tata Engg	    427	   0.61	41050  17.53     7.45</p>
<p>BSES Ltd	     172	   1.33	79900  13.74    40.32</p>
<p>IPCL		   114	   0.23	92300  10.52    10.52</p>
<p>ICICI		   64	   0.15     162900  10.43    12.22</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 13.20 percent on an annualised basis against 9.70 percent in the previous carry forward account ended Oct 5.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
